hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16359","Waki' narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hisham ibn 'Amir al-Ansari, he said: When the day of Uhud came, the people suffered wounds and severe hardship, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dig and widen, and bury two and three in the grave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, whom shall we put forward? He said: The most of them in gathering and taking of the Quran."
"16360","He said: Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, he said: The people used to buy gold with silver on credit until the giving, so Hisham ibn 'Amir came upon them and forbade them, and said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to sell gold with silver on credit, and informed us, or he said: and told us, that that is riba."
"16361","He said: Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from some of their shaykhs, he said: Hisham ibn 'Amir said to his neighbors: Indeed you go to men who were not more present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor more retentive of his hadith than I, and indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Between the creation of Adam and the establishment of the Hour there is no matter greater than the Dajjal."
"16362","He said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hisham ibn 'Amir, he said: Indeed you go to peoples who are not more knowledgeable of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than us; my father was killed on the day of Uhud, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dig and widen, and bury two and three in the grave, and put forward the most Quran of them, and my father was the most Quran of them, so he was put forward."
"16363","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: By Allah, between the creation of Adam and the establishment of the Hour there is no matter greater than the Dajjal."
"16364","He said: Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hisham ibn 'Amir, he said: They complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the wounds on the day of Uhud, and said: How do you command concerning our slain? He said: Dig and widen and do well, and bury in the grave two and three, and put forward the most Quran of them. Hisham said: So my father was put forward before two."
"16365","Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, Shu'bah said: I read it to him, he said: I heard Mu'adhah al-'Adawiyyah, she said: I heard Hisham ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake a Muslim beyond three nights, and if they cut off beyond three, then they are both deviating from the truth as long as they remain upon their cutting off, and the first of them to return, his preceding with the return is its expiation; and if he greets him and he does not return to him and returns his greeting to him, the angels return upon him and Satan returns upon the other; and if they both die upon their cutting off, they shall never gather in Paradise ever."
"16366","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mu'adhah, from Hisham ibn 'Amir, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake a Muslim beyond three nights, for they are both deviating from the truth as long as they remain upon their cutting off, and the first of them to return, his preceding with the return shall be an expiation for him; and if he greets and it is not accepted and his greeting is returned to him, the angels return upon him and Satan returns upon the other; and if they both die upon their cutting off, they shall never enter Paradise together ever."
"16367","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Amir said: The Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud and said: O Messenger of Allah, wounds and hardship have afflicted us, so how do you command us? He said: Dig and widen, and put two men and three in the grave. They said: Which of them shall we put forward? He said: The most Quran of them. He said: So my father 'Amir was put forward before a man or two."
"16368","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Hisham ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the head of the Dajjal from behind him is plaited, plaited; so whoever says: You are my lord, is tempted, and whoever says: You lie, my Lord is Allah, upon Him I rely, then it shall not harm him, or he said: then there is no trial upon him."
"16369","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: Hisham ibn 'Amir informed us, he said: My father was killed on the day of Uhud, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dig and widen and do well, and bury two and three in the grave, and put forward the most Quran of them; so my father was third of three, and he was the most Quran of them, so he was put forward."
"16370","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abu al-Dahma, from Hisham ibn 'Amir, he said: They complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what wounds were upon them, so he said: Dig and do well and widen, and bury two and three in the grave, and put forward the most Quran of them; so my father died and was put forward before two men."
"16371","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Hilal narrating, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from his father Hisham ibn 'Amir, he said: When the day of Uhud came, and he mentioned the hadith. He said:"
"16372","'Affan narrated to us, he said: I heard Jarir ibn Hazim narrating this hadith, from Humayd ibn Hilal, and he added in it, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, and he added in it: And deepen."
"16373","He said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd, meaning Ibn Hilal, from Hisham ibn 'Amir al-Ansari, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Between the creation of Adam and the establishment of the Hour there is no trial greater than the trial of the Dajjal."
"16374","He said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: Hisham ibn 'Amir came to al-Basrah and found them trading gold in their stipends, so he stood and said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling gold with silver on credit, and informed us, or he said: indeed that is riba."
"16375","He said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Dahma, from Hisham ibn 'Amir, he said: Indeed you pass beyond to a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they were not more enumerating nor more memorizing of his hadith than I, and indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Between Adam and the Day of Resurrection there is no matter greater than the Dajjal."
